 - Without an override, Ollama and llama.cpp loopback probes use short endpoint-specific budgets (150–250 ms); remote/LAN probes use 10 s. Generic model-list and proxy probes default to 10 s.
 - `discovery` requires provider-level `api`, except `discovery.type: proxy` (per-model wire auto-detected).
 
+To split one gateway's model list between providers without maintaining model ids:
+
+```yaml
+providers:
+  openai:
+    baseUrl: https://gateway.example.com
+    apiKey: GATEWAY_API_KEY
+    api: anthropic-messages
+    discovery:
+      type: openai-models-list
+      ownedBy: [openai]
+  anthropic:
+    baseUrl: https://gateway.example.com
+    apiKey: GATEWAY_API_KEY
+    api: anthropic-messages
+    discovery:
+      type: openai-models-list
+      ownedBy: [anthropic]
+```
+
+Use the wire API the gateway serves, independently of `owned_by`. `proxy` still
+selects each model's API from `supported_endpoint_types`; the owner filter does
+not change routing. Multiple owners can share a provider. Disjoint owner lists
+prevent the same discovery row from appearing under multiple providers.
+
+Set `discovery` explicitly on every provider in this layout. A `baseUrl` override
+alone can activate built-in endpoint discovery, which does not apply `ownedBy`
+and can import the gateway's entire model list, including with a `/v1` URL.
+Explicit discovery skips that built-in discovery path. Filtered caches are
+separate from unfiltered caches and from other owner lists.
+
+The filter applies only to discovered rows. Built-in catalog models and explicit
+`models` entries still merge as before, so a provider id that matches a built-in
+provider (`openai`, `anthropic`) also lists that provider's bundled roster. Set
+`discovery.authoritative: true` to list only what the gateway advertises. Use
+`modelOverrides` for metadata fixes without adding models that the gateway does
+not advertise.
+
+
 ### Remote compaction
 
 `remoteCompaction` is independently sufficient for an override-only provider.
